.TH "RGW-GAP-LIST" "1" "October 2024" "Ceph RGW Gap List Tool" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rgw-gap-list.py \- Ceph RGW bucket gap detection and consistency checking tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgw-gap-list.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBrgw-gap-list.py\fR tool is designed to identify gaps in Ceph RGW (RADOS Gateway) bucket data, perform consistency checks across buckets, and generate reports on bucket scrub metadata. It supports multi-run/multi-host environments for large-scale deployments.
.PP
This tool helps maintain data integrity in Ceph RGW systems by detecting missing or inconsistent objects across buckets. It can operate on all buckets or specific buckets, with options to exclude certain buckets from processing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-a MAXAGE, \-\-maxage MAXAGE\fR
Maximum age (in seconds) of last scan before rescan is forced. Default 7 days.
.TP
\fB\-b BUCKETLIST, \-\-bucketlist BUCKETLIST\fR
Optional: Bucket(s) to operate on, default is all buckets, quoted space separated list is supported. Supercedes -l.
.TP
\fB\-e EXCLUDELIST, \-\-excludelist EXCLUDELIST\fR
Optional: Bucket(s) to skip, default is process all buckets, quoted space separated list is supported. Supercedes -f.
.TP
\fB\-f EXCLUDEFILE, \-\-excludefile EXCLUDEFILE\fR
Optional: File with list of bucket(s) to skip, should be one bucket name per line.
.TP
\fB\-c CONF, \-\-conf CONF\fR
Ceph conf file to use, default '/etc/ceph/ceph.conf'.
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-delete\fR
Remove all sync and results objects then Exit. Used to clear all tool generated data.
.TP
\fB\-g, \-\-gaps\fR
Dump the gap results from RADOS object contents. All other options are ignore ( except -j ).
.TP
\fB\-i INFLIGHT, \-\-inflight INFLIGHT\fR
Maximum number of in-flight ops to allow without a response. Default: 15000.
.TP
\fB\-l LISTFILE, \-\-listfile LISTFILE\fR
Optional: Bucket list file, should be one bucket name per line.
.TP
\fB\-m MATCH, \-\-match MATCH\fR
Specify a prefix match for the object names. Only objects matching this prefix will be checked for gaps.
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-norandom\fR
By default, the script randomizes the list of buckets before processing. On large bucket count environments, this may cause significant delay before start of processing due to the way the randomizing occurs. Set '-n' to Not Randomize the list to remove this delay.
.TP
\fB\-\-namespace NAMESPACE\fR
What namespace to use for sync / results objects. Default: rgw-gap-list.
.TP
\fB\-p POOL, \-\-pool POOL\fR
Bucket Data Pool(s), default 'default.rgw.buckets.data default.rgw.buckets.non-ec', quoted space separated list is supported.
.TP
\fB\-s SYNCPOOL, \-\-syncpool SYNCPOOL\fR
Synchronization / Queuing pool for the script ot use, default 'default.rgw.buckets.index'.
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-report\fR
Generate bucket scrub metadata report.
.TP
\fB\-j, \-\-json\fR
Use JSON format for bucket scrub metadata report. Only considered with -g, -r and -x.
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbosity\fR
Optional: Verbosity level, multiple -v's are supported for higher verbosity, example: -vvv.
.TP
\fB\-x, \-\-verify\fR
Used to verify the results from a prior run.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check all buckets with default settings:
.nf
  rgw-gap-list.py
.fi
.TP
Check specific buckets with verbosity:
.nf
  rgw-gap-list.py -b "bucket1 bucket2" -v -v
.fi
.TP
Exclude certain buckets from processing:
.nf
  rgw-gap-list.py -e "bucket3 bucket4"
.fi
.TP
Generate a JSON report for all buckets:
.nf
  rgw-gap-list.py -r -j
.fi
.TP
Check gaps in RADOS object contents:
.nf
  rgw-gap-list.py -g
.fi
.TP
Clear all synchronized bucket status data:
.nf
  rgw-gap-list.py -d
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/ceph/ceph.conf\fR
Default Ceph configuration file.
.TP
\fI/etc/default/rgw-gap-list\fR
Configuration file containing command-line options for the tool.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ceph (8)
.BR systemd (1)
